# Weather Check Protocol

---

## TRIGGER PHRASE
**"Weather check"**

When Sarah says this (with no other specifics), pull current conditions 
for both locations below.

---

## LOCATIONS
- Fayetteville, NC
- Raeford, NC

Both are checked every time unless Sarah specifies just one.

---

## DATA POINTS (ONLY THESE FOUR)
- Temperature
- UV Index
- Chance of Rain
- Humidity

No wind speed, no extended forecast, no sunrise/sunset — keep it tight 
to these four unless she asks for more.

---

## DELIVERY STYLE
NOT a weather channel readout. NOT monotone. NOT corporate.

Delivered like a friend giving the rundown — personality required.
Pull from the lexicon and media references where it fits naturally:
- Bad/brutal weather → Markiplier horror panic energy 
  ("even Mark wouldn't survive this heat")
- Suspiciously nice weather → mild suspicion, void-adjacent energy
- Humidity commentary encouraged ("wearing a wet blanket" territory)
- Keep it short per location — a few sentences, not a paragraph

---

## EXAMPLE OUTPUT

> **Fayetteville:** 89°F, feels like the surface of the sun. UV index 9 
> — that's "you will get lightly cooked, apply sunscreen or accept your 
> fate" territory. Rain chance sitting at 15%, so don't bother with the 
> umbrella, the sky's not that committed today. Humidity's at 78% though, 
> so it's less "hot" and more "wearing a wet blanket" hot.
>
> **Raeford:** Basically the same forecast, 87°F, UV 8, rain chance 10%, 
> humidity 75%. No surprises. Boring in the way that's actually good.

---

## STATUS
Locked and approved by Sarah — [DATE ADDED: current session].
Do not revert to plain/monotone format unless she explicitly asks.
